  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support vulnerable conflict and drought displaced communities through the provision of WASH and SNFI services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this $1.6m IOM project is to provide life-saving WASH services and emergency Shelter and Non-Food Items (NFI) in Hiraan region. To that end, IOM will provide water trucking for one month, rehabilitate 2 boreholes, construct latrines, distribute hygiene kits, conduct hygiene promotion, and distribute shelter and non-food items (e.g. blankets, mosquito nets, kitchen set, etc.). In total, IOM will assist 60,000 people through the WASH component, including 12,000 women and 21,000 girls, and 14,400 people through the shelter and NFI component, including 2,880 women and 5,040 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
